And the `Point` type includes pressure. drag.points: Point[] — no problem.

Also, should we render the draft stroke while dragging? Currently, in drag mode we don't set draftRef, so no line is shown while dragging. In the release-time decision approach, the user sees the component following the finger (no line). On release over B → the line appears. I think that's fine — actually cleaner.

Hmm, wait. But let me reconsider once more whether we should show the line during the gesture when the pointer is over another component… no. Keep it simple. The README can document: "Drag a component to move it; press on a component and release over another to wire them."

Actually — that last part is a great interaction: "press on A, release over B = wire A→B". It's discoverable and documented.

